WEBVTT

00:12.053 --> 00:14.389
♪ See the daylight ♪

00:15.223 --> 00:17.392
♪ Covering the sky ♪

00:18.852 --> 00:22.230
♪ Hear the wind say ♪

00:22.313 --> 00:26.484
♪ No matter what you do, my friend ♪

00:26.568 --> 00:29.696
♪ You know the world
Still needs your light ♪

00:29.779 --> 00:32.449
♪ Let it just shine ♪

00:32.532 --> 00:38.246
♪ You'll be free
From all the things you used to be ♪

00:43.585 --> 00:48.590
DOONA!

00:50.884 --> 00:51.968
[Doona] "I'm glad."

00:53.553 --> 00:54.888
That's what she said?

00:57.307 --> 00:58.641
That she was glad?

00:58.683 --> 00:59.768
EPISODE 3
SPRING BREEZE

00:59.851 --> 01:03.396
Yeah. What do you think that means,
from a girl's point of view?

01:03.480 --> 01:04.564
[Doona] Mmm…

01:05.106 --> 01:07.400
Well, I think it could mean two things.

01:09.652 --> 01:10.653
Number one,

01:11.905 --> 01:13.948
"I'm glad nothing's going on,

01:14.032 --> 01:16.242
'cause I plan on keeping you
all to myself."

01:16.326 --> 01:17.660
"I like you, Won-jun."

01:19.537 --> 01:21.164
Number two, "Doona?"

01:21.664 --> 01:24.417
"Mmm. I'm not really a fan of Doona's."

01:25.168 --> 01:27.045
"Well, good thing
you're not seeing her then."

01:27.128 --> 01:28.213
[scoffs]

01:28.296 --> 01:29.672
Or it's neither of those two.

01:30.882 --> 01:32.717
[Doona] Hey, are you stupid?

01:32.801 --> 01:34.052
Of course it's number one

01:34.636 --> 01:36.596
Why would a girl like Jin-ju
like me, you know?

01:39.432 --> 01:40.809
Why wouldn't she like you?

01:41.351 --> 01:42.769
Because I'm a fan.

01:43.394 --> 01:44.270
[chuckles]

01:45.396 --> 01:46.981
What's with the smile on your face, huh?

01:48.775 --> 01:51.778
It's not that, um,
don't think I'm a great guy,

01:51.861 --> 01:55.240
but we've known each other
for a while, and I don't want to ruin it.

01:57.450 --> 01:59.536
I think that you
might be overthinking it.

02:00.870 --> 02:02.288
Just live in the present, huh?

02:03.123 --> 02:06.084
Hey, it's not like Jin-ju is a…
a mind reader, you know?

02:06.167 --> 02:07.335
I'm definitely not.

02:08.336 --> 02:11.089
In the chance, you end up getting hurt,
you can cry on my shoulder, hmm?

02:11.172 --> 02:13.466
- [chuckles]
- That's what real friends are for, huh?

02:30.525 --> 02:31.442
Hmm.

02:36.322 --> 02:37.824
THE ART OF MATHEMATICS

02:41.035 --> 02:43.580
FOR SOPHOMORES
THE ART OF MATHEMATICS

02:50.628 --> 02:52.172
[gentle music playing]

02:55.466 --> 02:57.468
[girls laughing]

03:00.722 --> 03:03.850
Oh! Won-jun, Won-jun, come quick.

03:03.933 --> 03:04.767
- Okay.
- Close that.

03:04.851 --> 03:05.768
All right.

03:05.852 --> 03:08.646
[robotic voice] Five. Four. Three.

03:08.730 --> 03:10.857
- Two. One.
- [sighs]

03:10.940 --> 03:11.983
[camera clicks]

03:14.694 --> 03:17.322
- [sighs]
- [robotic voice] Five. Four. Three.

03:17.906 --> 03:19.449
Two. One.

03:19.532 --> 03:20.700
[camera clicks]

03:20.783 --> 03:22.285
[chuckles]

03:22.368 --> 03:24.120
- Okay, what's next?
- [robotic voice] Five.

03:24.204 --> 03:26.080
- Four. Three.
- Finger hearts, Won-jun.

03:26.164 --> 03:27.999
[robotic voice] Two. One.

03:28.082 --> 03:29.792
- [laughs]
- [camera clicks]

03:29.876 --> 03:31.044
What are you doing?

03:31.628 --> 03:33.171
Hold on. Do it right.

03:33.254 --> 03:36.049
- Like this. There you go.
- [robotic voice] Five.

03:36.132 --> 03:39.969
Four. Three. Two. One.

03:40.053 --> 03:41.095
[camera clicks]

03:42.263 --> 03:44.265
[tender music playing]

03:54.192 --> 03:57.862
There's a rumor
that you and I might be together.

03:57.946 --> 03:59.197
Uh-huh, I heard.

03:59.280 --> 04:00.156
But it's not true,

04:00.740 --> 04:02.408
'cause we're just friends, right?

04:02.492 --> 04:06.579
Uh, what do you tell everyone
whenever they ask you

04:06.663 --> 04:08.289
what the deal is between us?

04:08.998 --> 04:09.874
You go first.

04:10.833 --> 04:12.043
What do you tell people?

04:12.126 --> 04:14.796
Well… so…

04:15.880 --> 04:17.215
I just say that we're close.

04:19.008 --> 04:20.301
That we get along well.

04:23.263 --> 04:24.931
Like soulmates kind of.

04:26.766 --> 04:29.227
[gentle music plays]

04:30.603 --> 04:31.604
Oh, really?

04:32.397 --> 04:34.482
I like that. Soulmates, huh?

04:34.565 --> 04:36.067
[both chuckle]

04:47.620 --> 04:49.622
[Jin-ju] Mmm, this one came out good.

04:50.707 --> 04:52.083
[Won-jun] Only you look good.

04:52.709 --> 04:55.461
[Jin-ju chuckles]
No, you look good in it too!

05:11.352 --> 05:12.645
[distant camera clicks]

05:58.107 --> 05:59.317
[sighs]

06:04.030 --> 06:06.491
[man] Happy birthday. I'll be in touch.

06:08.201 --> 06:11.120
[gentle piano music playing]

06:18.503 --> 06:20.213
[breathing heavily]

06:20.296 --> 06:21.464
[gentle music builds]

06:25.802 --> 06:27.637
[music becomes tense]

06:43.694 --> 06:45.696
[faucet running]

06:47.698 --> 06:48.658
[sighs]

06:51.119 --> 06:51.994
[sighs]

06:57.166 --> 06:58.000
[sighs]

07:06.926 --> 07:07.802
[exhales]

07:08.845 --> 07:10.430
[mysterious music playing]

07:10.513 --> 07:11.806
[crying]

07:19.021 --> 07:21.607
[panting]

07:36.914 --> 07:39.041
[Jin-ju] Here you go.
Apologies for the wait.

07:39.125 --> 07:41.085
We have a lot of drink orders
at the moment.

07:41.169 --> 07:42.086
Please enjoy.

07:42.587 --> 07:45.089
[calm music plays]

08:06.736 --> 08:09.071
[woman] I'm so sorry.
I spilled some coffee over there.

08:09.155 --> 08:11.491
Ah, okay. Um, I… Well, I can get it.

08:11.574 --> 08:13.910
Oh. Thank you, Won-jun.

08:25.838 --> 08:26.923
Jin-ju?

08:28.508 --> 08:29.592
Hmm?

08:30.176 --> 08:31.928
Do you have any plans tomorrow?

08:32.720 --> 08:33.721
Uh…

08:34.805 --> 08:37.433
Well, the cherry blossoms are out.
But you probably can't go.

08:37.517 --> 08:38.643
[Jin-ju] No, wait, uh…

08:41.771 --> 08:42.772
Okay.

08:43.564 --> 08:44.440
[sighs]

08:44.524 --> 08:45.525
Okay, great, then.

08:49.779 --> 08:51.781
[gentle music playing]

08:54.492 --> 08:55.451
[sighs]

08:57.036 --> 08:57.954
[chuckles]

08:58.037 --> 08:59.121
[dishes clink]

09:04.293 --> 09:05.169
[chuckles]

09:21.435 --> 09:22.520
[door closes]

09:22.603 --> 09:23.563
[door beeps]

09:35.616 --> 09:37.660
[footsteps]

09:42.915 --> 09:44.584
Doona, where are you?

09:45.543 --> 09:46.544
[knocks]

09:47.712 --> 09:48.879
Hey, Doona, are you there?

09:48.963 --> 09:50.214
[knocking]

09:52.466 --> 09:53.843
Is that you knocking? Doona!

09:58.889 --> 10:00.516
- Doona!
- [knocking]

10:02.810 --> 10:03.644
[knocking]

10:03.728 --> 10:05.563
[Won-jun] Doona, are you…
are you in there?

10:06.063 --> 10:07.148
I can't get out.

10:07.231 --> 10:08.524
[doorknob rattles]

10:09.108 --> 10:10.234
Can you break down the door?

10:10.318 --> 10:12.069
[Won-jun] Just hang on
for a little longer.

10:12.153 --> 10:14.572
[footsteps running]

10:14.655 --> 10:16.741
[grunts]

10:27.001 --> 10:29.003
[Doona breathing heavily]

10:38.429 --> 10:40.431
[emotional music playing]

10:56.489 --> 10:58.115
[Doona sighs]

11:12.380 --> 11:13.214
[grunts]

11:22.390 --> 11:24.016
What are you thinking about right now?

11:27.186 --> 11:28.104
You're so sexy.

11:29.271 --> 11:32.316
A man who fixes bathroom doors,
it's so sexy and cool.

11:32.400 --> 11:34.902
Ah, you're so incorrigible, you know that?

11:35.945 --> 11:36.862
[Won-jun grunts]

11:37.363 --> 11:38.489
No, seriously.

11:39.699 --> 11:41.283
It's probably from not having a father.

11:42.201 --> 11:44.954
So this kind of thing
has always been a fantasy of mine.

11:45.705 --> 11:47.331
Ah, so, um, is he not around?

11:47.998 --> 11:48.833
Mm-mm.

11:48.916 --> 11:50.751
I also lost my father when I was young.

11:55.089 --> 11:56.632
I never had one to begin with.

11:57.967 --> 12:00.177
I guess life must've been
really hard for you too, then.

12:00.261 --> 12:01.387
It wasn't.

12:03.013 --> 12:03.931
Believe it or not,

12:04.598 --> 12:06.517
I found it really convenient.

12:06.600 --> 12:08.561
I could imagine my father
to be anyone I'd like.

12:10.438 --> 12:12.189
But do you know what's really hard?

12:12.982 --> 12:15.151
It's not the people
who were never there to begin with.

12:15.735 --> 12:18.529
But it's when you lose the people
that were always there from the start.

12:19.029 --> 12:21.365
That's enough to drive you really insane.

12:25.953 --> 12:26.954
Look at that.

12:27.037 --> 12:28.789
Of course these disappeared too.

12:31.375 --> 12:32.668
Oh, I, uh…

12:32.752 --> 12:36.005
I saw some cigarettes in your cabinet
when I was looking for the tools.

12:37.673 --> 12:38.507
Oh, those?

12:49.435 --> 12:50.436
[sighs]

12:51.687 --> 12:52.938
These aren't mine.

12:55.107 --> 12:57.359
I would never smoke crappy cigarettes.

12:58.277 --> 12:59.361
[Won-jun] Hey, Doona.

13:00.446 --> 13:02.281
Uh, should we go outside?

13:04.033 --> 13:05.868
Instead of smashing bottles
over people's heads,

13:05.951 --> 13:07.870
this is a better alternative.
Just give it a shot.

13:09.747 --> 13:10.831
Grab hold of the hammer.

13:11.791 --> 13:12.625
Like this.

13:20.674 --> 13:23.302
- [game chimes]
- [robotic voice] Faster!

13:23.385 --> 13:26.722
You gotta whack hard to score. Think
of everything you hate, then smash it.

13:26.806 --> 13:30.392
[robotic voice] Faster!
Hee-hee-hee! Getting angry?

13:34.104 --> 13:35.648
There's a pattern, you see? Take a look.

13:36.148 --> 13:38.275
[robotic voice]
That hurts! That hurts! That hurts!

13:38.359 --> 13:40.569
- Don't hit me! Don't hit me!
- You're doing great!

13:40.653 --> 13:43.322
- [game chiming]
- [robotic voice] That hurts! That hurts!

13:43.405 --> 13:44.740
[Won-jun] It's fun, right?

13:44.824 --> 13:45.991
Oh, there's one!

13:46.075 --> 13:47.952
Here. Here. There.

13:48.035 --> 13:50.371
- [robotic voice] That hurts!
- [game chiming]

13:50.454 --> 13:52.206
- [robotic voice] Great job!
- Whoa!

13:52.289 --> 13:53.249
You did good.

13:53.332 --> 13:55.334
- I wanna go again.
- [Won-jun] Hmm.

13:55.918 --> 13:57.294
- Go for it.
- [coin clangs]

13:57.378 --> 13:59.296
[robotic voice] That hurts! That hurts!

13:59.380 --> 14:01.757
- [game chiming]
- [Won-jun] That's it.

14:01.841 --> 14:04.260
- [robotic voice] Don't hit me!
- [game chiming]

14:04.343 --> 14:05.511
[robotic voice] That hurts!

14:05.594 --> 14:07.179
YOUR SCORE

14:11.642 --> 14:13.561
[emotional music playing]

14:13.644 --> 14:14.854
[robotic voice] That hurts!

14:14.937 --> 14:17.606
[theme music plays]

14:24.238 --> 14:26.156
- Boo! Boo!
- [Won-jun] How did I miss that?

14:26.699 --> 14:28.284
[both laughing]

14:28.367 --> 14:29.410
[Doona squeals]

14:30.327 --> 14:31.453
Hey! Oh!

14:32.663 --> 14:33.747
- [Won-jun] Oh!
- [squeals]

14:37.960 --> 14:40.379
- [Won-jun] Get in there!
- [Doona] Whoo!

14:40.462 --> 14:41.839
[laughs]

14:43.883 --> 14:45.676
[Doona] Give it to me! Give it to me!

14:45.759 --> 14:47.678
[both laughing]

14:47.761 --> 14:48.762
[Won-jun] Ah!

14:50.472 --> 14:51.640
[Doona] Wanna play some more?

15:05.487 --> 15:06.447
[Won-jun] Go ahead.

15:07.239 --> 15:09.617
- [Doona grunts]
- [both cheering]

15:10.743 --> 15:12.620
[Doona] I'm beat.

15:12.703 --> 15:14.121
[Doona grunts]

15:17.541 --> 15:18.375
Hey.

15:20.210 --> 15:21.629
You should lie on your back.

15:23.672 --> 15:25.299
It's really pretty. Look.

15:30.304 --> 15:32.932
[both panting]

15:36.435 --> 15:37.519
[Won-jun chuckles]

15:39.146 --> 15:40.648
[Doona] Why are you laughing?

15:41.440 --> 15:43.525
[Won-jun] Well, it's just…
What are you calling pretty?

15:43.609 --> 15:44.735
I can't see a single star.

15:45.319 --> 15:47.154
It's completely overcast right now.

15:48.530 --> 15:51.700
- It's probably gonna rain tonight.
- [sighs] Do you think so?

15:55.120 --> 15:56.455
It's a beautiful sky.

15:57.748 --> 15:58.999
I don't care if it rains.

16:01.627 --> 16:02.503
[sighs]

16:05.506 --> 16:07.675
Thank you for everything, Won-Jun.

16:08.717 --> 16:10.052
It was so much fun.

16:10.636 --> 16:11.595
I had fun too.

16:12.471 --> 16:15.933
I can't remember the last time
I let go and had so much fun like this.

16:18.060 --> 16:18.978
[sighs]

16:22.231 --> 16:24.483
I asked Jin-ju to come with me
and see the cherry blossoms.

16:24.566 --> 16:25.442
[gasps]

16:27.069 --> 16:28.821
Really? She said yes?

16:29.780 --> 16:31.615
Uh… oh, uh, well, I…

16:31.699 --> 16:33.325
I kind of thought she'd say no, but yeah.

16:33.409 --> 16:35.494
To be honest,
I was surprised she said yes.

16:37.246 --> 16:40.124
Don't run away from her.
You can't keep doing that, okay?

16:41.875 --> 16:42.710
[grunts]

16:42.793 --> 16:44.128
Okay, I… I won't.

16:59.560 --> 17:00.769
[sighs]

17:04.481 --> 17:05.399
[sighs]

17:14.450 --> 17:15.284
[sighs]

17:21.331 --> 17:22.332
[birds chirping]

17:22.416 --> 17:23.542
[Won-jun] Hmm.

17:24.585 --> 17:25.419
Hmm.

17:25.919 --> 17:28.088
Mmm, the weather is…

17:28.172 --> 17:29.298
SEOUL WEATHER CLEAR

17:29.381 --> 17:30.466
…clear and sunny.

17:32.009 --> 17:32.968
[chuckles]

17:34.803 --> 17:36.055
[exhales]

17:36.138 --> 17:38.140
[gentle music playing]

17:53.280 --> 17:54.615
- Won-jun!
- Oh. Oh.

17:55.282 --> 17:57.785
[Jin-ju chuckles softly] Let's go.

17:59.203 --> 18:01.705
[gasps] Oh, they're so pretty!

18:01.789 --> 18:04.583
They are, aren't they?
There's so many cherry blossoms falling.

18:04.666 --> 18:05.834
[Jin-ju] Mm-hmm.

18:05.918 --> 18:06.960
Oh, right, hey.

18:07.044 --> 18:11.340
Kook Su-jin's apartment complex
has gorgeous cherry blossoms, remember?

18:11.423 --> 18:12.591
Ah, I definitely remember.

18:12.674 --> 18:14.176
That's when we skipped a day of school

18:14.259 --> 18:16.178
and went
to the playground in front of his place.

18:16.261 --> 18:18.055
[laughs]

18:18.138 --> 18:20.265
What? We didn't skip a whole day.

18:20.349 --> 18:22.267
[chuckles] You were scared to miss class,

18:22.351 --> 18:24.812
so we went back after 20 minutes
so they wouldn't count you out.

18:24.895 --> 18:26.647
- [clears throat]
- [chuckles]

18:26.730 --> 18:31.985
Lee Won-jun wouldn't ever arrive late
for a class, let alone skip, hmm?

18:32.569 --> 18:33.862
You're really something else.

18:33.946 --> 18:35.114
[chuckles]

18:36.740 --> 18:38.033
[Won-jun] Wow.

18:38.117 --> 18:39.326
[Jin-ju] Wow.

18:39.409 --> 18:40.327
[chuckles]

18:43.580 --> 18:44.456
[gasps]

18:44.540 --> 18:46.083
- Hey, the other day--
- There was some--

18:46.166 --> 18:47.751
You go ahead. Please, be my guest.

18:47.835 --> 18:49.795
[chuckles] No, you go first.

18:50.921 --> 18:53.423
Uh, so the other day, I found this game,

18:53.507 --> 18:55.843
the one you liked to play
when we were back in high school.

18:55.926 --> 18:57.386
Seriously? [gasps]

18:57.469 --> 18:59.471
Oh, I totally miss playing that.

18:59.555 --> 19:02.307
I haven't played it here in Seoul.
So did you play it?

19:02.808 --> 19:05.269
Uh, actually, no. Doona was playing it.

19:05.769 --> 19:07.062
She never played it before.

19:07.146 --> 19:09.189
Well, everything is a first for her.

19:10.440 --> 19:11.441
Hmm.

19:13.610 --> 19:15.612
Um, what were you going to say earlier?

19:15.696 --> 19:16.697
Well, um,

19:18.282 --> 19:19.616
I forgot already. Hmm.

19:20.284 --> 19:22.286
[emotional music playing]

19:24.454 --> 19:25.289
[Jin-ju] Oh.

19:27.541 --> 19:30.127
- It's starting to rain.
- Ah.

19:32.713 --> 19:33.547
[Jin-ju] Ah.

19:44.600 --> 19:45.893
[sighs]

19:53.692 --> 19:54.610
[sighs]

19:58.238 --> 19:59.072
[Se-hun] Hey, Jin-ju!

20:00.824 --> 20:01.950
Se-hun?

20:07.789 --> 20:10.375
A towel. Where is it?

20:11.793 --> 20:13.879
- [Won-jun] Oh, here.
- [Se-hun] Oh, thanks, man.

20:13.962 --> 20:15.589
Here, put this over you.
You're pretty wet.

20:15.672 --> 20:16.715
Oh, thanks.

20:21.428 --> 20:22.763
[phone vibrating]

20:25.641 --> 20:26.475
YUN-TAEK

20:26.558 --> 20:28.393
Is it all right
if I take this call right now?

20:28.477 --> 20:29.519
Oh, please do. No worries.

20:31.188 --> 20:32.564
Hey, Yun-taek.

20:32.648 --> 20:34.858
[Yun-taek] Won-jun, when are you back?
We got pizza.

20:34.942 --> 20:36.693
It was two for one, so we got four.

20:36.777 --> 20:38.237
- Uh…
- [Se-hun] I know that voice.

20:38.320 --> 20:41.156
Hey, are you talking
to Seo Yun-taek by chance?

20:41.240 --> 20:43.992
Uh, yes. How did you know it was Yun-taek?

20:44.076 --> 20:47.579
[Se-hun] Wow, it really is
such a small world.

20:47.663 --> 20:49.790
Who would've guessed
Won-jun's friend from back home

20:49.873 --> 20:53.335
and my best friend
would, uh, connect like this?

20:53.418 --> 20:55.254
Amazing, right? [laughs]

20:55.337 --> 20:59.508
Jin-ju, what can I say about Se-hun?
I may be biased because he's my friend,

20:59.591 --> 21:02.344
but that's one impressive bastard there,
for real. I'm serious.

21:02.427 --> 21:04.137
- First of all, he's tall.
- You're too kind.

21:04.221 --> 21:06.723
He's good-looking. Oh… and wealthy.

21:06.807 --> 21:09.601
And don't forget,
he's freaking amazing at sports,

21:09.685 --> 21:11.478
which is why his body is amazing.

21:11.561 --> 21:13.063
You look at his legs, whoa!

21:13.146 --> 21:16.358
- You lucked out for sure, Jin-ju. No joke!
- [Se-hun] Hey, don't be that guy.

21:16.441 --> 21:18.402
He's always like this when he's drunk.
Ignore him.

21:18.485 --> 21:20.279
- It's totally fine.
- [can slams on table]

21:22.990 --> 21:25.867
Anyways, so are
the two of you dating or what?

21:26.535 --> 21:28.036
Uh, I wouldn't say that. We're just--

21:28.120 --> 21:30.205
[Se-hun] I'd say
we're more like soulmates.

21:30.289 --> 21:32.165
We get along so well, it's special.
[chuckles]

21:32.833 --> 21:33.917
Uh-huh.

21:34.001 --> 21:35.085
[Yun-taek] Oh!

21:35.168 --> 21:38.964
[laughs] Then you should be dating.
You have to date now.

21:39.047 --> 21:40.716
[laughs] You should kiss her!

21:40.799 --> 21:43.218
- Oh! Huh?
- Hey, Yun-taek. Eat the food.

21:43.302 --> 21:44.177
Here.

21:44.261 --> 21:46.513
Because if you keep speaking,
you'll die of starvation.

21:46.596 --> 21:48.682
Oh, wow. Really?

21:49.308 --> 21:51.393
You finally acknowledged me
by my name just now.

21:51.476 --> 21:53.270
Does that mean
you know I actually exist?

21:53.353 --> 21:55.814
- Oh, this is amazing!
- Man, you really need a tranquilizer.

21:55.897 --> 21:58.692
- You seriously talk too much.
- [Yun-taek] Am I talking too much?

21:59.192 --> 22:00.610
You can talk too, you know?

22:00.694 --> 22:03.613
Besides, you can't rain on this parade,
because Dream Sweet knows who I am!

22:03.697 --> 22:05.490
Doona, I'll go get
some ice cream for everyone.

22:06.199 --> 22:07.034
Okay.

22:07.117 --> 22:09.202
[Yun-taek] Let's celebrate! Woo-hoo!

22:09.703 --> 22:11.621
Cheers! [laughs]

22:11.705 --> 22:14.750
You see, this guy over here,
when we did our national service…

22:14.833 --> 22:16.835
[tender music playing]

22:33.602 --> 22:35.896
[Won-jun panting]

22:42.819 --> 22:43.945
Oh, you're here,

22:44.029 --> 22:45.989
my soulmate.

22:46.948 --> 22:47.866
[chuckles]

22:52.371 --> 22:53.205
[Jin-ju sighs]

22:53.288 --> 22:55.957
It looks like I have to retake my exams.

22:57.626 --> 23:01.004
I wanted us to go to university together,
but now it won't happen.

23:01.838 --> 23:02.672
Mmm.

23:04.299 --> 23:06.218
Wow, it's getting really cold.

23:15.352 --> 23:17.729
[tender music playing]

23:34.454 --> 23:36.123
Is that a little better now?

23:43.004 --> 23:43.922
Not really.

23:45.465 --> 23:47.300
I still feel so cold, Won-jun.

24:04.776 --> 24:06.695
- [door opens]
- [bell jingles]

24:06.778 --> 24:08.530
[footsteps approaching]

24:11.324 --> 24:12.325
[Won-jun] Hmm?

24:17.247 --> 24:19.082
Your taste is similar to a grandma's.

24:19.583 --> 24:21.376
For example,
like the toe socks you're wearing.

24:22.461 --> 24:23.753
Aren't you cold at all?

24:23.837 --> 24:25.964
Hmm. Don't worry. I'm immune to the cold.

24:26.548 --> 24:27.757
[chuckles]

24:29.843 --> 24:30.677
Whoa.

24:33.263 --> 24:35.807
- These cherry blossoms are different.
- What is it?

24:36.433 --> 24:37.767
Look at the petals.

24:37.851 --> 24:40.896
Yangjin and Seoul's are different
from each other, but so are these ones.

24:40.979 --> 24:42.272
[chuckles]

24:44.524 --> 24:46.067
Well, should I tell you why that is?

24:46.610 --> 24:47.569
Do you know?

24:49.321 --> 24:50.989
Those weren't cherry blossoms at all, huh?

24:51.072 --> 24:53.450
Those were actually peach blossoms,
you dummy.

24:53.533 --> 24:56.286
Oh. Where did you learn that?

24:56.786 --> 24:58.705
I guess
I'm just smarter than you, Mr. Lee.

24:59.206 --> 25:01.583
You should address me
as your teacher from now on.

25:01.666 --> 25:02.626
Yes, Teacher.

25:03.210 --> 25:04.461
You go ahead, okay?

25:05.545 --> 25:07.589
- What are you doing?
- I'm gonna smoke.

25:08.673 --> 25:10.217
Uh, I can stay with you if you want.

25:10.300 --> 25:13.220
Mm-mm. The ice cream will melt otherwise.

25:14.137 --> 25:15.972
- Throw this away, will you?
- Yep.

25:17.474 --> 25:18.350
All right, then.

25:23.647 --> 25:25.649
[footsteps approaching quickly]

25:34.699 --> 25:37.786
- [Won-jun] Here we are. Ice cream.
- [Yun-taek] Whoa, ice cream.

25:39.079 --> 25:39.996
[Se-hun] Thanks a lot.

25:40.622 --> 25:41.706
[Yun-taek] There you go.

25:42.707 --> 25:45.418
- Here you go. It's your favorite.
- Oh, thank you so much.

25:45.919 --> 25:48.004
- Hey, Won--
- [Yun-taek] Doona, get your ice cream!

25:49.798 --> 25:51.424
[Doona] What were you talking about?

25:51.508 --> 25:52.968
[Yun-taek] Huh? Oh, yeah, yeah.

25:53.051 --> 25:54.344
All right, so,

25:55.178 --> 25:57.222
the wild boar is charging right at me.

25:57.722 --> 25:59.641
And they're really fast, you know?

26:00.141 --> 26:02.477
I obviously couldn't outrun it.
I knew it immediately.

26:02.561 --> 26:04.437
So I thought, "I'll jump on its back!"

26:05.480 --> 26:07.440
I went for it and landed on its back.

26:07.941 --> 26:09.776
- But I was turned around!
- [chuckles]

26:09.859 --> 26:12.529
[Yun-taek] So I'm on backwards,
and this thing never even slows down.

26:12.612 --> 26:14.864
People are shouting,
"Hey, where are you going?"

26:14.948 --> 26:17.409
"I'll return on boar-back. Don't worry!"

26:17.492 --> 26:19.411
So then I grabbed its tail,
you know, to steer.

26:19.494 --> 26:22.289
- [Se-hun] Come on. Stop lying.
- [Yun-taek] Of course it's a lie, jackass.

26:22.372 --> 26:24.833
How could it possibly be true?
Seriously, dude.

26:24.916 --> 26:26.793
[Se-hun scoffs] You're so drunk.

26:27.294 --> 26:30.213
- So, just flirting right now?
- So far, yes, just flirting.

26:30.297 --> 26:31.464
Mmm.

26:31.548 --> 26:32.924
Jin-ju's really cute, right?

26:33.508 --> 26:34.342
Huh?

26:34.426 --> 26:35.635
[laughs]

26:37.429 --> 26:38.763
Hell yeah. [laughs]

26:39.389 --> 26:41.349
Anyway, congratulations, man.

26:49.232 --> 26:50.900
Doona, can we hang out again sometime?

26:53.069 --> 26:54.195
Whenever you'd like.

27:00.035 --> 27:01.828
- [upbeat music playing]
- [cheering]

27:01.911 --> 27:03.246
[boy] Over here!

27:05.457 --> 27:07.375
Let's go, literature team!

27:07.459 --> 27:09.044
Pass it! Block them!

27:09.127 --> 27:11.004
[cheering]

27:16.676 --> 27:18.678
[Jin-ju] Come on! Whoo!

27:18.762 --> 27:21.014
- They're gonna end up fighting.
- There's no way.

27:21.097 --> 27:23.558
Won-jun would never do that.
He'd give up the ball in that case.

27:23.642 --> 27:25.101
[grunts]

27:26.311 --> 27:28.188
- [boy 2] Go! Go get him!
- [boy 3] All right!

27:28.855 --> 27:29.939
Come on!

27:30.023 --> 27:30.940
[grunts]

27:31.733 --> 27:33.652
- [Jin-ju] Whoo!
- [sighs]

27:33.735 --> 27:36.738
[Jin-ju] Yes, Se-hun! Whoo!

27:36.821 --> 27:37.864
[boy] You got this.

27:40.241 --> 27:41.409
KOR LIT
CIV ENG

27:41.493 --> 27:42.994
- [Jin-ju] Oh.
- Yeah.

27:43.703 --> 27:45.413
Hey, Jin-ju, could you
hold onto this for me?

27:45.997 --> 27:47.540
Oh, sure. Uh…

27:47.624 --> 27:49.250
Go, literature team!

27:49.876 --> 27:52.462
- [boy 4] Come on, Se-hun. Go get him!
- Hey, Jeong!

27:54.506 --> 27:56.049
[girl] There it goes! There it goes!

27:56.132 --> 27:57.300
Block it!

27:57.384 --> 27:59.719
[cheering and applause]

27:59.803 --> 28:02.097
[Doona] Whoo!

28:02.180 --> 28:03.431
Whoo!

28:03.515 --> 28:05.600
- Whoo!
- Yay.

28:08.103 --> 28:09.020
Whoo!

28:09.604 --> 28:11.272
[cheering]

28:12.440 --> 28:14.275
- Take care of that leg.
- Good job, everyone.

28:14.901 --> 28:15.819
All right.

28:18.530 --> 28:20.281
- Good work, guys!
- [Won-jun] Thanks.

28:23.159 --> 28:25.036
Jin-ju, are you coming with me
to lunch today?

28:25.120 --> 28:26.496
Oh, actually…

28:26.579 --> 28:28.331
There's a new pasta place
across the street.

28:29.165 --> 28:30.709
- Let's go together.
- Uh…

28:31.876 --> 28:34.129
I should head back to school
because I still have class.

28:34.212 --> 28:35.296
[Se-hun] Oh.

28:35.380 --> 28:36.631
How about just us?

28:38.466 --> 28:40.176
- Mm-hmm. All right.
- [chuckles]

28:40.260 --> 28:41.928
- Let's play again, okay?
- All right.

28:42.011 --> 28:44.097
[gentle piano music playing]

28:45.056 --> 28:46.015
Well, I'll get going.

28:46.641 --> 28:47.475
Let's eat, hmm?

28:52.939 --> 28:54.691
So is this new pasta place good?

28:55.608 --> 28:57.610
[gentle music continues]

28:57.736 --> 28:58.778
[sighs]

29:08.496 --> 29:10.457
[Doona] Did you miss class because of me?

29:10.540 --> 29:12.083
[Won-jun] I didn't wanna go anyway.

29:15.295 --> 29:16.838
You let that boy take her away.

29:17.422 --> 29:18.798
You could lose her for good.

29:18.882 --> 29:20.759
Listen, Miss Teacher,
how could I lose her, hmm?

29:20.842 --> 29:21.968
She isn't mine to lose, okay?

29:22.051 --> 29:23.636
What are you saying?

29:23.720 --> 29:25.013
'Cause from what I see,

29:25.096 --> 29:27.265
you and Jin-ju
definitely have feelings for one another,

29:27.348 --> 29:29.184
but you guys aren't doing anything.

29:29.267 --> 29:31.352
At least tell her how you feel
before you give up.

29:31.436 --> 29:33.146
Just watching you both
just makes me get mad.

29:34.856 --> 29:35.899
I did try already.

29:36.900 --> 29:39.110
I told her I had feelings for her
a long time ago.

29:39.194 --> 29:40.236
She knew how I felt.

29:42.280 --> 29:43.114
She did?

29:43.698 --> 29:44.866
Yeah.

29:44.949 --> 29:47.202
At the time, I thought
she had feelings too.

29:57.295 --> 29:58.296
I really like you.

30:07.597 --> 30:08.890
[line ringing]

30:18.191 --> 30:20.485
[robotic voice] Sorry, the number
you're trying to reach…

30:20.568 --> 30:22.195
[Won-jun] Is everything okay?

30:25.448 --> 30:26.533
[Jin-ju] Sorry.

30:26.616 --> 30:29.118
I've just been super busy.
I'll talk to you later.

30:33.873 --> 30:34.791
MAYBE

30:36.626 --> 30:39.921
COULD WE

30:46.386 --> 30:50.223
COULD YOU COME OUT FOR

30:52.517 --> 30:55.645
- [girl] This could feed two dozen people.
- [girl 2] We can definitely finish this.

30:55.728 --> 30:58.064
- [Jin-ju] Of course we can eat it.
- [girl] Of course we can!

30:58.982 --> 31:00.733
- [Jin-ju] Let's do it!
- [girls laughing]

31:01.901 --> 31:03.903
[somber music playing]

31:09.993 --> 31:10.994
[Won-jun] Okay.

31:14.289 --> 31:15.331
Take care.

31:25.008 --> 31:26.092
We lost touch after that,

31:26.175 --> 31:28.678
and we didn't see each other
for over a year.

31:32.974 --> 31:34.309
It was my fault, really.

31:36.144 --> 31:37.186
What was?

31:37.270 --> 31:40.356
Well, making assumptions
about someone else's feelings towards you.

31:41.566 --> 31:44.319
And overstepping the mark
without any real conviction to do so.

31:44.986 --> 31:45.862
'Cause of that,

31:46.738 --> 31:48.907
at that time,
it cost me a very good friend.

31:52.410 --> 31:54.704
But luckily, it's water under the bridge.

31:54.787 --> 31:58.333
And now I'm just really happy that we
can be friends once again, you know?

32:00.293 --> 32:01.377
So I'm grateful.

32:05.173 --> 32:08.176
So in that case, um,
your teachings can officially stop.

32:10.511 --> 32:12.764
[sighs] Wow,
I can't believe I just got fired.

32:13.389 --> 32:14.223
What a bummer.

32:14.307 --> 32:16.392
- And I never got paid for my services.
- [chuckles]

32:20.063 --> 32:21.272
[phone ringing]

32:23.775 --> 32:24.859
SE-HUN

32:28.279 --> 32:30.865
Uh… I'll be right back, okay?

32:49.050 --> 32:50.259
[indistinct noise]

32:55.932 --> 32:57.141
Who's there?

32:57.225 --> 32:58.476
[footsteps]

32:58.559 --> 33:00.436
[ominous music playing]

33:01.521 --> 33:02.480
[crowd cheering]

33:04.357 --> 33:05.608
[cameras clicking]

33:14.826 --> 33:15.910
[breathing shakily]

33:23.835 --> 33:25.837
Doona really must be getting
super bored, huh?

33:25.920 --> 33:27.755
She always wants to hang out with you.

33:27.839 --> 33:31.426
She never had friends until now.
I feel a little sorry for her.

33:32.885 --> 33:35.555
She really seems
to rely on you a lot lately.

33:36.139 --> 33:39.267
Nah, she just likes to make fun of me.
I'm not much to rely on.

33:40.059 --> 33:42.270
- Should we get some chips?
- Mm-hmm.

33:49.152 --> 33:51.487
You should give yourself
a little more credit, Won-jun.

33:53.489 --> 33:54.949
You're totally reliable.

33:57.076 --> 33:59.454
[man] Sorry for the wait.
I'll check you out now.

33:59.996 --> 34:00.872
[beeps]

34:00.955 --> 34:03.124
[Yun-taek] Oh, that's right.
It's April Fools' Day.

34:04.333 --> 34:06.669
So did you all, um, tell some lies today?

34:06.753 --> 34:09.297
Let's hear 'em all now.
What have you guys got?

34:10.465 --> 34:11.299
I love you.

34:12.425 --> 34:13.634
Like a lot.

34:14.177 --> 34:15.470
Oh, I love you too.

34:15.970 --> 34:18.306
- You jerk, I should kick you in the face!
- Ah! Calm down!

34:18.389 --> 34:19.265
[Won-jun laughs]

34:19.348 --> 34:21.059
Someone told me today he liked me.

34:26.397 --> 34:28.149
I still haven't responded to him.

34:28.775 --> 34:29.609
Why not?

34:31.903 --> 34:34.030
'Cause I'm not sure how I feel about him.

34:38.242 --> 34:39.327
[Jin-ju] It's really weird.

34:40.244 --> 34:42.747
When there's someone
that I'm into a whole lot,

34:44.165 --> 34:46.793
as soon as they approach me,
I totally lose my nerve.

34:48.169 --> 34:50.630
I worry they'll be disappointed somehow.

34:52.632 --> 34:54.801
Especially when they learn who I am.

35:04.310 --> 35:05.978
[chuckles] What's wrong?

35:07.063 --> 35:08.648
Weren't we supposed to lie?

35:08.731 --> 35:10.525
[chuckles] Jeez, you guys!

35:10.608 --> 35:12.777
Seriously, you should see your faces.

35:12.860 --> 35:15.154
- [laughs]
- Huh? I'm so impressed by your acting.

35:15.238 --> 35:18.449
Is that like method acting?
Just now, I was totally absorbed by her.

35:18.533 --> 35:21.494
Ugh, Doona's not a good influence.
You should stop hanging out with her.

35:21.577 --> 35:24.497
I thought that was awesome, Jin-ju.
Good job, huh? [chuckles]

35:25.915 --> 35:27.875
So next is, um, Miss Doona.

35:29.127 --> 35:32.463
What's your lie, Doona? It's gonna be hard
to follow Jin-ju's act, right?

35:32.547 --> 35:35.007
I'm being stalked by a guy,
and I don't know who he is.

35:36.384 --> 35:39.846
- What a weird concept for a lie.
- [Doona] Believe me. I wish it were a lie.

35:43.975 --> 35:45.309
YOU'RE PRETTY

35:46.394 --> 35:47.270
It isn't.

35:47.353 --> 35:48.354
Doona, what is this?

35:51.691 --> 35:52.817
[man] You're so pretty.

35:54.485 --> 35:55.444
He's among us now.

36:02.160 --> 36:05.163
What the hell?
Whoa! Who the hell was that?

36:05.746 --> 36:06.831
Oh, wait. What?

36:07.373 --> 36:08.332
[Yun-taek] You creep!

36:08.416 --> 36:10.543
[suspenseful music playing]

36:14.755 --> 36:16.174
Hey you! Stop!

36:16.257 --> 36:17.675
- [Yun-taek] Hey!
- Won-jun!

36:18.342 --> 36:19.260
[Yun-taek] Hey!

36:19.343 --> 36:20.970
Stop that punk! You bastard!

36:21.804 --> 36:23.931
Get him! That… Ugh!

36:24.015 --> 36:25.516
- Get him!
- [Jin-ju] He turned that way!

36:28.102 --> 36:30.104
- Oh! Oh!
- [Jin-ju] I've got it! Ah!

36:30.188 --> 36:32.231
- Are you all right?
- I've got his bag. Yes, thanks.

36:32.899 --> 36:34.609
- [Yun-taek] Are you okay?
- Oh, we got it.

36:34.692 --> 36:36.986
We need to get used to this.
There's gonna be more stalkers.

36:39.572 --> 36:40.573
[Won-jun grunts]

36:41.490 --> 36:43.075
[both grunting]

36:43.159 --> 36:44.368
[man] Hey, let go of me!

36:45.703 --> 36:47.872
You're busted! I got you! [grunts]

36:47.955 --> 36:49.790
[man] Ah! Let go!

36:49.874 --> 36:51.459
[both grunting]

36:51.542 --> 36:53.586
[Yun-taek] Hey! There he is! You bastard!

36:54.253 --> 36:56.088
[Jeong-hun and Yun-taek] Son of a bitch!

36:56.172 --> 36:58.799
- Won-jun, are you okay?
- [Yun-taek] Who do you think you are?

36:59.717 --> 37:01.802
- Hey, help me get a hold of this creep!
- [man grunts]

37:01.886 --> 37:04.096
Hold him. Hold him. Hold him.
How dare you?

37:06.015 --> 37:07.934
[man panting]

37:08.017 --> 37:10.061
[suspenseful music playing]

37:23.491 --> 37:24.700
This isn't good.

37:25.993 --> 37:26.911
- What is it?
- What?

37:28.496 --> 37:30.414
- [gasps]
- He's seriously a little shit.

37:31.040 --> 37:34.877
I just did it out of pure curiosity.
I swear that's what it was!

37:34.961 --> 37:37.129
She came into the convenient store
and I got excited.

37:37.213 --> 37:38.589
I worship her, guys, truly!

37:44.720 --> 37:46.305
We should handle this ourselves.

37:46.389 --> 37:47.890
Exactly what do you have in mind?

37:47.974 --> 37:49.892
We should beat his ass.
That's what he deserves.

37:51.477 --> 37:52.937
I'll do it here and now.

37:54.689 --> 37:56.691
I'll do it until he's
on the verge of being dead.

37:58.609 --> 38:02.405
Maybe I'll go for his head first.
I bet that would feel really good.

38:09.453 --> 38:11.163
I've always wanted
to smash someone's head.

38:11.247 --> 38:12.415
- [man] No!
- Wait, Doona.

38:12.498 --> 38:14.417
[all] Whoa!

38:14.500 --> 38:16.544
[Doona breathing shakily]

38:16.627 --> 38:18.838
[gentle piano music playing]

38:21.090 --> 38:22.842
[whimpering]

38:26.595 --> 38:27.430
[gasps]

38:30.391 --> 38:33.144
Oh, wow. She didn't do it.

38:33.227 --> 38:35.313
Oh, thank goodness,
someone's thinking rationally.

38:37.398 --> 38:38.232
- Ah!
- Listen.

38:39.108 --> 38:41.277
I'll kill you if you say one more word,
you got it?

38:41.861 --> 38:42.903
[man] I'm truly sorry.

38:43.404 --> 38:44.280
[grunts]

38:49.910 --> 38:51.162
[sighs]

38:52.455 --> 38:53.873
[Doona breathing shakily]

38:56.709 --> 38:59.420
[Jin-ju] Do you really think
it's all right not to call the police?

39:00.671 --> 39:02.256
Doona is dead set against it.

39:03.382 --> 39:04.759
She must have her reasons.

39:06.052 --> 39:09.221
Are you all right?
You look like you're hurt pretty ba--

39:09.305 --> 39:10.431
Really, it's okay.

39:17.396 --> 39:20.024
So, it looks like
I'm gonna be leaving home soon.

39:20.107 --> 39:21.567
That's why I'm working so much.

39:22.443 --> 39:25.196
My dad was always against it,
but I'm moving.

39:25.988 --> 39:27.948
- I did wonder what was going on.
- [chuckles]

39:28.657 --> 39:29.533
Really?

39:31.577 --> 39:32.953
[phone chimes]

39:41.754 --> 39:42.630
[sighs]

39:58.145 --> 39:58.979
DAD

39:59.063 --> 40:00.898
WHY AREN'T YOU BACK HOME YET, YOU BITCH?

40:00.981 --> 40:03.859
YOU THINK I SENT YOU TO COLLEGE
SO YOU CAN FOOL AROUND WITH MEN?

40:03.943 --> 40:04.944
TEXT ME BACK RIGHT NOW

40:05.027 --> 40:05.861
I'M ON MY WAY

40:07.488 --> 40:08.364
[sighs]

40:22.711 --> 40:23.754
[chuckles]

40:24.547 --> 40:26.549
[tender music playing]

41:02.126 --> 41:03.043
[grunts softly]

41:04.795 --> 41:05.754
[grunts softly]

41:11.510 --> 41:12.636
[sighs]

41:17.892 --> 41:18.851
[phone vibrates]

41:26.609 --> 41:28.235
YOU'VE GOTTEN BETTER AT LYING

41:28.319 --> 41:30.821
STOP CONTACTING ME AND WAIT QUIETLY

41:35.409 --> 41:36.243
[Won-jun sighs]

41:50.883 --> 41:51.967
[sighs]

41:58.516 --> 42:00.518
[footsteps approaching]

42:02.353 --> 42:03.521
[Doona] Won-jun, you're here.

42:05.356 --> 42:07.608
- Yeah, hey.
- Why are you down here?

42:07.691 --> 42:09.610
Oh, I couldn't sleep at all.

42:10.694 --> 42:12.196
Can I have one of your beers?

42:22.540 --> 42:24.291
Why don't you sit down for a second?

42:42.935 --> 42:45.020
We got a copy
of the stalker's identification,

42:45.104 --> 42:46.272
the memory card,

42:46.355 --> 42:48.899
even a written statement
promising to never do it again.

42:49.400 --> 42:51.193
We got everything
that we thought you'd need.

42:51.277 --> 42:53.571
We also went to his home
and wiped out both of his computers

42:53.654 --> 42:55.155
of any pictures or videos,

42:55.239 --> 42:56.991
and he also agreed to quit his job.

42:57.950 --> 43:00.661
We told his parents and the store manager
what happened as well.

43:02.997 --> 43:05.958
So now, I'll give you everything, and, uh,

43:07.418 --> 43:10.546
well, when you feel ready to present this
at the police, you can at your own time.

43:10.629 --> 43:11.630
It's your choice.

43:12.339 --> 43:13.257
Okay, thanks.

43:16.218 --> 43:17.636
I appreciate your help.

43:21.557 --> 43:24.602
So, um, it must've been scary
having to deal with that alone.

43:26.729 --> 43:27.563
It wasn't.

43:33.527 --> 43:34.528
Hey, Doona.

43:36.822 --> 43:40.784
It's okay to be scared, you know?
It's a lot better than you getting hurt.

43:44.997 --> 43:47.374
Actually,
I never wanna see you get hurt ever.

43:47.958 --> 43:50.252
What I hope for you
is to be loved by everyone again.

43:59.553 --> 44:00.429
[sighs]

44:06.435 --> 44:08.145
I think I'm ready to go to bed now.

44:09.146 --> 44:10.272
I need to sleep.

44:43.472 --> 44:45.432
Do you mind if we hold hands?

44:47.434 --> 44:49.895
If you don't like it,
you can pull your hand away.

44:57.820 --> 45:00.656
[gentle music plays]
